  "body_markdown": "About us\n\nmeet Dr. ChrisMeet The TeamLivewell DifferenceOffice TourTechnologyJoin Our Team\n\nservices\n\ndCOEFull Mouth ReconstructionSedation Dentistry\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nSmile MakeoverPorcelain VeneersNo Prep VeneersGum RecontouringTeeth WhiteningDental Bonding\n\nImplant Dentistry\n\nDental ImplantsSingle ImplantsImplant BridgesAll-on-X ImplantsLocator-Retained Dentures\n\nRestorative Dentistry\n\nDental CrownsInlays & OnlaysDental BridgesTooth-Colored Fillings\n\nOral Surgery\n\nBone GraftingRidge AugmentationTooth ExtractionSinus LiftWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nOrthodontics\n\nInvisalignBraces\n\nGeneral Dentistry\n\nPreventive DentistryPreventive CleaningGum TherapyRoot Canal Therapy\n\nTMJ TreatmentDental Emergencies\n\nnew patient\n\nfirst visit & new examInsurance & FinancingBlog\n\nOur work\n\nSmile GalleryTestimonials\n\nContact\n\ncall (703) 690-0102Request An Appointment\n\nBook Now\n\n703-690-0102\n\nLivewell Difference\n\nmeet Dr. Chris\n\nMeet The Team\n\nJoin Our Team\n\nOffice Tour\n\nTechnology\n\nServices\n\nFull Mouth Reconstruction\n\nDCOE\n\nTMJ Treatment\n\nDental Emergencies\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nPreventive\n\nDental Bridges\n\nRoot Canal\n\nProfessional Dental Cleaning\n\nScaling & Root Planing\n\nAll General Dentistry services\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nNo Prep Veneers\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nGum Recontouring\n\nAll Cosmetic Dentistry Services\n\nSingle Implants\n\nImplant Bridges\n\nAll-on-X Implants\n\nLocator-Retained Dentures\n\nAll Implant Dentistry Services\n\nWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nTooth Extraction\n\nSinus Lift\n\nBone Grafting\n\nRidge Augmentation\n\nInvisalign\n\nBraces\n\nAll Orthodontics Services\n\nDental Crowns\n\nTooth-Colored Fillings\n\nDental Bonding\n\nInlays & Onlays\n\nAll Restorative Dentistry Services\n\nNew Patient\n\nfirst visit & new exam\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nBlog\n\nTestimonials\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nCALL US: (703) 690-0102\n\nBOOK AN APPOINTMENT\n\n\n# No Prep Veneers In Livewell Dental\n\n\nLittle-to-no enamel removal\n\nNatural smile design\n\nVirtual review first\n\nStart Your Virtual Consultation\n\n\n## You Want a Better Smile. You Don’t Want to Regret the Process.\n\n\nVeneers can feel exciting until one question gets in the way:\n\nWill healthy teeth have to be shaved down?\n\nThat hesitation is reasonable. Enamel is valuable, and once it is removed, it cannot be put back. At Livewell Dental, we begin with a more careful question: can we create the smile you want while preserving as much natural tooth structure as possible?\n\nA permanent decision\n\n‍Your smile should be improved with care, not rushed into irreversible treatment\n\nA conservative first look\n\n‍We study your tooth shape, enamel, bite, and smile goals before recommending veneers.\n\nA clearer path forward\n\n‍Sometimes no prep is possible. Sometimes another option is better. Either way, you should know why.\n\nThe goal is not just a prettier smile. It is a smile you can feel good about choosing.\n\n\n## Meet Your Guide\n\n\n\n### Dr. Chris\n\n\nDr. Chris approaches cosmetic dentistry with one priority first: protect what is healthy.\n\nA smile is not just a row of teeth. It is part of your face, your expression, your bite, and the way you move through life. Before recommending veneers, Dr. Chris looks at enamel, tooth position, facial balance, lip support, color, gum shape, and long-term function.\n\nUCSF-trained dentist\n\n‍Advanced clinical foundation with a thoughtful, evidence-based approach.\n\nKois Center GraduateTraining focused on complete care, function, and long-term stability.\n\nFellow, Academy of General DentistryA distinction earned through extensive continuing education.\n\n\n## What Are No Prep Veneers?\n\n\nThin Porcelain Layer\n\nNatural Edge Shape\n\nNo prep veneers are thin porcelain veneers placed with little to no removal of healthy enamel. For the right patient, they can improve the shape, color, size, and balance of the smile by adding carefully designed porcelain instead of aggressively reducing natural teeth.\n\nA brighter smile without an artificial look.\n\nMore even edges, proportions, and symmetry.\n\nA fuller look for small, narrow, or worn teeth.\n\nA broader smile when teeth sit slightly inward.\n\n\n## Are You the Right Candidate for No Prep Veneers?\n\n\nNo prep veneers work best when your smile has room to accept a small amount of added porcelain. That usually means the teeth can be enhanced without looking thick, heavy, or unnatural.\n\nTeeth that feel small or narrow\n\n‍No prep veneers may add fuller shape and better balance.\n\nA smile that feels slightly set back\n\n‍Porcelain can sometimes bring the smile forward in a natural way.\n\nWorn or uneven edges\n\n‍Careful design can restore length, shape, and symmetry.\n\nHealthy enamel\n\n‍Strong enamel helps create a more predictable bond.\n\nFind Out If No Prep Is Right for You\n\nIf no prep is not the right fit, that is not bad news. It simply means your smile may need a different conservative path.\n\n\n## Virtual consultaion\n\n\nBegin Online Review\n\n01\n\n\n### Upload Your Photos\n\n\nSend a few clear, natural photos from your phone. No filters. No special lighting. Just a real look at your smile.\n\nFull smile photo\n\nResting face photo\n\nSide or angle photo\n\nClose-up smile photo\n\n02\n\n\n### Share your smile goals\n\n\nTell us what bothers you and what you hope to change.\n\nMaybe you want a brighter smile.\n\nMaybe your teeth feel small or uneven.\n\nMaybe you have old bonding.\n\nMaybe you like the idea of veneers, but you are nervous about shaving healthy teeth.\n\n03\n\n\n### Get personal feedback\n\n\nOnce we have your photos and your goals, your part is done.\n\nNow we go to work.\n\nDr. Chris will review your smile and help you understand whether no prep veneers may be worth exploring — or whether another conservative path may make more sense.\n\nThis is not a final diagnosis. It is a thoughtful first step.\n\n\n## See What’s Possible Before Anything Is Permanent\n\n\nIf you have been thinking about veneers but hesitating because you do not want healthy teeth shaved down, start with a careful first look.\n\nSend your photos. Share what you want to change. Dr. Chris will help you understand whether no prep veneers may be possible, or whether another conservative path makes more sense.\n\nSchedule Your Consultation\n\nCall Us\n\n\n## eLab Technology: Where Digital Science Meets Dental Art\n\n\nBecause You Deserve Better Than “Close Enough”\n\nNatural-looking veneers depend on details most people never see. Shade, translucency, texture, edge shape, facial balance, and how the teeth reflect light all matter.\n\nAt Livewell Dental, digital planning and eLab-style communication help Dr. Chris and the lab design veneers with more precision before anything is finalized. The goal is simple: a smile that looks polished, but still belongs to your face.\n\nShade with intention\n\n‍We study color so the result does not look flat, opaque, or overly white.\n\nShape with restraint\n\n‍The design is planned to avoid a bulky or overbuilt look.\n\nDetails before delivery\n\n‍Photos, scans, and planning help guide the final ceramic work.\n\nAm I a candidate for no prep veneers?\n\nYou may be a good candidate if your teeth are slightly small, narrow, worn, or set back, and there is room to add porcelain naturally. If your teeth are crowded, prominent, very dark, or heavily restored, another option may be more appropriate.\n\nWill no prep veneers look bulky?\n\nThey can look bulky if they are forced into the wrong case. That is why planning matters. Dr. Chris evaluates your tooth position, smile shape, enamel, and bite before deciding whether no prep veneers make sense.\n\nCan veneers fix small or narrow teeth?\n\nYes, in many cases veneers can improve tooth size, shape, and smile width. No prep veneers are often most successful when the smile can be enhanced by adding carefully designed porcelain. For broader cosmetic planning, you may also want to review our smile makeover page.\n\nWhat if I am not a no prep candidate?\n\nThat does not mean you are out of options. Depending on your smile, Dr. Chris may recommend teeth whitening, dental bonding, gum recontouring, alignment, minimal-prep veneers, or a more complete cosmetic plan.\n\nHow long do no prep veneers last?\n\nWith good planning, strong bonding, proper bite management, and regular dental care, porcelain veneers can last many years. Longevity depends on your enamel, bite, habits, and how well the veneers are maintained.\n\nWhat photos should I send for a virtual consultation?\n\nSend a full smile photo, a relaxed resting photo, a side or angle photo, and a close-up smile photo. You can also include an inspiration photo if there is a smile style you like. No filters or special lighting are needed.\n\nCan I get veneers if I grind my teeth?\n\nGrinding does not disqualify you from veneers, but it does need to be addressed before and after treatment. Uncontrolled grinding puts veneers at risk of chipping or failing early. At Livewell, every case begins with a bite evaluation. If grinding is a factor, Dr. Chris will discuss how to protect your result long-term before a single veneer is placed.\n\n\n### Frequently Asked Questions\n\n\nContact Us\n\n\n### Reimagine your dental experience\n\n\n\n### address\n\n\n9027 Silverbrook Rd Ste. F\n\nFairfax Station, VA 22039\n\n\n### Contact\n\n\n\n### Hours\n\n\nMon-Tue: 8am-5pm\n\nWed-Thu: 8am-4pm\n\nFri: 8am-1pm\n\n\n### Connect\n\n\nServing Fairfax Station and the Greater Northern Virginia Area\n\nCopyright © TEXT-YEAR Livewell Dental\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nTerms of Service\n\nCookie Policy\n\nHIPAA Disclosure\n\nConsent Preferences",
